329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Microfinance Institutions \(MFIs\) play a vital role in promoting financial inclusion and economic development by providing access to credit, savings, insurance, and financial services to underserved populations. They empower individuals, especially women, to start or expand small businesses, improve their income, and enhance decision-making power, which helps reduce poverty and promote gender equality. MFIs also encourage savings, build financial resilience, and foster entrepreneurship, leading to job creation and stronger local economies. By supporting financial literacy and stability, they help households manage expenses, reduce vulnerability to shocks, and plan for the future. Beyond financial gains, MFIs generate social impact by improving the overall well-being and quality of life within communities.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
