/T (Rural finance has been crucial for poverty alleviation, agricultural growth, and rural enterprise development, especially when delivered through sustainable, market-oriented programs. However, access remains unequal, with rural communities still underserved compared to urban areas. Policy reforms have improved efficiency, but challenges persist in deepening financial access, ensuring agricultural credit, and strengthening rural institutions.)
